lexical extraction
├── when extracting typescript lexically
│   ├── it matches the native extraction
│   └── it reports parameterized tests identically
├── when decoys hide in comments and strings
│   └── it matches the native extraction
├── when aliases bind describe and it
│   ├── it matches the native extraction
│   ├── it reports aliased each identically
│   ├── it resolves module var and exported aliases identically
│   ├── it ignores for header aliases identically
│   ├── it bounds a ten thousand link chain identically
│   ├── it drops source derived patterns between files
│   └── it ignores non module aliases identically
├── when fuzzing random test files
│   ├── it emits aliases and parameterized tests
│   └── it never diverges from the native extraction
├── when extracting rust lexically
│   └── it matches the native extraction
├── when fuzzing random rust files
│   └── it never diverges from the native extraction
├── when a raw name profile extracts declarations
│   ├── it nests tests by explicit bracket spans
│   └── it preserves line breaks while blanking comments
├── when source uses syntax outside the profile
│   └── it documents possible silent divergence
├── when a scaffolded file is checked lexically
│   ├── it reports no findings for hostile titles
│   ├── it merges missing skeletons idempotently
│   ├── it reports todo markers identically to the native backend
│   └── it ignores string literal markers identically to the native backend
├── when a lexical profile is malformed
│   └── it refuses to load
└── when the scanner cannot account for the source
    └── it fails closed
